<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">League of Lezhë</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1444</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The League of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lezhe">Lezhë</a> was an alliance of Albanian noble families founded at Lezhë in March 1444 under the leadership of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a>, with Venetian-protected Lezhë as its meeting place. Members such as the Dukagjini and the Crnojević of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeta-region">Zeta</a> pledged men and money for war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, though the alliance soon weakened through rivalries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/league-of-lezhe.jpg" alt="League of Lezhë" width="320" height="610" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ahmet Q. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:League_of_Lezh%C3%AB,_1448-1468.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
